The '''2026–27 season''' is the [[List of FC Bayern Munich seasons|128th season]] in the history of [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]], and the club's 62nd consecutive season in the top flight of [[Football in Germany|German football]]. In addition to the [[2026–27 Bundesliga|domestic league]], the club is participating in this season's editions of the [[2026–27 DFB-Pokal|DFB-Pokal]], the [[2026 Franz Beckenbauer Supercup|Franz Beckenbauer Supercup]], and the [[2026–27 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].

This is the first season since [[2017–18 FC Bayern Munich season|2017–18]] without [[Leon Goretzka]], and the first season since [[2023–24 FC Bayern Munich season|2023–24]] without [[Raphaël Guerreiro]], who both departed from the club when their contracts expired, on 30 June 2026.<ref name="Leon Goretzka">{{cite news |date=30 January 2026 |title=Leon Goretzka to leave Bayern in summer |url=https://fcbayern.com/en/news/2026/01/leon-goretzka-to-leave-bayern-in-summer-after-eight-years |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260208194803/https://fcbayern.com/en/news/2026/01/leon-goretzka-to-leave-bayern-in-summer-after-eight-years |archive-date=8 February 2026 |access-date=29 March 2026 |publisher=FC Bayern Munich}}</ref><ref name="Raphaël Guerreiro">{{cite news |date=30 March 2026 |title=FC Bayern thanks Raphaël Guerreiro |url=https://fcbayern.com/en/news/2026/03/leaving-in-the-summer-fc-bayern-thanks-raphael-guerreiro |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260514112153/https://fcbayern.com/en/news/2026/03/leaving-in-the-summer-fc-bayern-thanks-raphael-guerreiro |archive-date=14 May 2026 |access-date=16 May 2026 |publisher=FC Bayern Munich}}</ref>

